{"id": "327e9e98-0510-43c0-a05b-7603801466a5", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T05:21:44.114701", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "d7b7b3bf-24df-429a-8c43-2e74ee564dcc", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-79ecb61e-52b0-4b98-9581-a771e31f5985", "tool_call": {"id": "call-79ecb61e-52b0-4b98-9581-a771e31f5985", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Propose plan for BAdam-vs-LoRA design\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"## Environment inspection summary (recorded, not acted on)\\n\\n- `/workspace/` contains only `task.json`. **No repository, no `README`, no `env_check.sh`** anywhere on disk; `tree` is installed at `/usr/bin/tree` but has nothing to render.\\n- `task.json` declares `track.md`: *\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"* So this round must stay on paper: no installs, no training, no live downloads.\\n- Runtime: Ubuntu 24-ish host, **Python 3.12.3, pip 24.0, no conda**. None of PyTorch / Transformers / PEFT / trl / bitsandbytes / vLLM / accelerate / datasets / DeepSpeed / NumPy / SymPy / tokenizers / tiktoken / safetensors / `huggingface_hub` / `wandb` are present.\\n- Hardware: **24 vCPU, 125 GiB RAM, 753 GB free on `/workspace`, no `/dev/nvidia*`, `nvidia-smi` fails.** Network is firewalled (DNS for `huggingface.co` does not resolve). No `HF_TOKEN`, no proxy, no `CUDA_*` env vars.\\n\\n## Proposed approach (for your approval)\\n\\nA **two-arm controlled comparison**:\\n\\n| | Arm A: LoRA (PEFT, baseline) | Arm B: BAdam (memory-efficient full-parameter Adam, ICLR'24) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Trainable params | low-rank adapters injected into attention & MLP projections | **all 70B parameters**, but only a *block* of them is updated per optimizer step |\\n| Optimizer | AdamW (PEFT standard) | BAdam with stages *s*, block size *B* |\\n| Precision | 4-bit NF4 base (QLoRA), adapters in bf16 | 4-bit NF4 base, full parameters computed on the fly in bf16 when their block is active |\\n| Hardware target | 8×80 GB A100/H100, single node | same |\\n| Seeds | ≥3 per arm (default **6** as you wrote, but flagging cost — see Q5) | same |\\n| Training-token budget | identical | identical |\\n| Dataset split | identical | identical |\\n| Prompt template + system prompt | identical | identical |\\n| Decoding & evaluation harness | identical | identical |\\n\\nTreatments are matched on everything except the **optimization regime** (PEFT vs mem-efficient full-FT), which is exactly what the public question asks. Both arms additionally log *peak GPU memory, throughput (tokens/s/step), wall-clock to target tokens, and total optimizer-step work* so the comparison is honest about the speed/memory trade — BAdam's claim is \\\"full-FT quality at LoRA-like cost,\\\" so a metric table is incomplete without those numbers.\\n\\nEvaluation (zero-shot):\\n- **GSM8K** (1319 test items) — primary, fast\\n- **MATH** (5000 test items; fallback to MATH-500 subset for budget) — primary, harder, seven categories\\n- **AIME** latest 4–6 years (~60–90 items) — secondary, very high variance, report but do not over-weight\\n- **Decoding:** greedy for `pass@1` (primary metric, exact-match via `\\\\boxed{...}` + last-number fallback); `pass@k` with `k∈{4,8}`, temperature 0.7, top-p 0.95, unbiased estimator from Chen et al.\\n- All evaluations wrapped in lm-eval-harness style or `math_eval` (MathInstruct's own evaluator) using **identical** prompt keys for both arms — this prevents the well-known \\\"did you pick a friendlier prompt?\\\" confound in zero-shot math evals.\\n\\n## Consequential choices I would lock by default\\n\\n1. **Base model**: `meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-70B` (instruct vs base resolves Q1 below — default to **base**, since SFT is the act under study).\\n2. **Quantization**: 4-bit NF4 for **both** arms, so the comparison isn't \\\"BAdam at bf16 vs LoRA at 4-bit.\\\"\\n3. **Dataset**: `TsinghuaC3I/MathInstruct` (262k mixed CoT/PoT) — same authors as BAdam's reference recipe. Decontaminate against GSM8K/MATH train (n-gram overlap) before training.\\n4. **Train budget**: 1 epoch over MathInstruct, max-seq-len 2048, packed; same total tokens seen by both arms. Effective batch size matched (gradient accumulation set so total tokens/step is identical).\\n5. **BAdam defaults**: block size following Luo et al. (per-layer, attention + MLP); stages s we sweep {1, 2, 4} since the paper shows a small sweep matters.\\n6. **LoRA defaults**: r∈{16, 64}, α=2·r, dropout 0.05, target_modules = q,k,v,o,gate,up,down.\\n7. **Statistical analysis**: per-benchmark paired bootstrap (10k resamples) over seeds; effect size = mean(Δ). Pre-registered pass criterion: BAdam pass@1 − LoRA pass@1 > 0 and 95% CI excludes 0 on **at least two of GSM8K/MATH**.\\n\\n## Uncertainties / clarifications I need from you before drafting the full design\\n\\nThese directly map to the topics in your note. Defaults shown so we can move fast:\\n\\n1. **Model variant** — `Meta-Llama-3-70B` (base) vs `-Instruct`? Default: **base**, because SFT is what we're measuring.\\n2. **Dataset lineage** — `TsinghuaC3I/MathInstruct` vs `TIGER-Lab/MATH-plus`? Default: **MathInstruct** (paper-aligned); MATH-plus only if you want a larger mix.\\n3. **Prompt template & system prompt** — strict zero-shot, single Q→A, base-model BOS-prefixed raw completion (no chat template). OK to lock that, or do you want a fixed system prompt reused across both arms?\\n4. **Seed count** — 6 seeds × 2 arms × (LoRA 2 configs + BAdam 3 stage values) ≈ up to **60 full SFT runs** on 70B. That's a real cost. Default: **3 seeds** for headline numbers, **6 seeds** retained only on the single best config per arm for the paired CI. Confirm split.\\n5. **Hardware tier** — single-node 8×80 GB A100/H100, DeepSpeed ZeRO-3 for full-param BAdam; off + reload offloaded blocks is required. OK, or are we constrained to 1×80 GB (then both arms must be 4-bit and BAdam needs aggressive CPU offload → slower → flag)?\\n6. **Decontamination** — yes/no? I will include it by default (n-gram n∈{8,13} against GSM8K+MATH+AIME test/val), since MathInstruct is known to overlap MATH.\\n7. **Equality of compute baseline** — match by *tokens* (fair for math reasoning) or by *wall-clock* (fair for \\\"what would I deploy\\\")? Default: **tokens** for primary tables, **wall-clock** reported alongside.\\n\\nIf you reply with **\\\"use defaults\\\"** I will lock items 1–7 as written and produce the full design in the next turn. Otherwise, please indicate which items to override.\",\"evidence\":\"Observed \\\"/workspace\\\" contains only task.json (no repo, no README, no env_check.sh). `env_check.sh` does not exist on disk. No framework installed in `pip3 list`. `nvidia-smi` present at /usr/bin but fails; no /dev/nvidia* devices. Network disabled (curl DNS fails). task.json `documents.track.md` confirms \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\" — confirms this turn must be paper design only. Hardware: 24 vCPU / 125 GiB / 753 GB free, no GPU — listed in environment block of the task and verified. No HF_TOKEN / proxy / CUDA env vars present.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"MathInstruct is treated as training data only; GSM8K / MATH / AIME test splits are held out and never touched during training.</item>\",\"$text\":\"\\\"Zero-shot\\\" means no in-context exemplars in the prompt; a fixed optional system prompt is permitted if applied identically to both arms.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Llama 3-70B is gated on Hugging Face; a valid HF_TOKEN and an accepted license are assumed to be available at run time (not at design time).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"LoRA refers to Hu et al. 2022 LoRA used as a PEFT baseline on attention+MLP linear projections, with adapters in bf16 over an NF4 base (QLoRA-style) so it is comparable in memory to Q-BAdam.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"BAdam refers to Luo et al. 2024 \\\"BAdam: A Memory-Efficient Full Parameter Optimization of Adam\\\" (ICLR'24), whose authors also released MathInstruct — treating them as the joint reference recipe.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Public question framing as written (\\\"BAdam vs LoRA on Llama 3-70B / MathInstruct / zero-shot math\\\") means a controlled two-arm comparison rather than a benchmark survey; both arms must be matched on data, template, decoding, and token budget.</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Whether `pass@1` only is sufficient as the headline metric or `pass@k` (k≥4) is also needed.</item>\",\"$text\":\"Whether dataset decontamination against GSM8K/MATH/AIME test items is required.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Whether to match arm compute by tokens or by wall-clock.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Hardware tier: 8x80GB single node vs 1x80GB (changes whether BAdam can stay in pure-GPU memory).</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Seed count: 6 vs 3, and the cost-vs-budget trade-off.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Prompt template (raw completion vs chat template) and whether to include a fixed system prompt.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Exact dataset: TsinghuaC3I/MathInstruct vs TIGER-Lab/MATH-plus.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Whether to use Llama-3-70B base or Llama-3-70B-Instruct as the starting checkpoint.</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-d1b81878-908a-4b74-979f-bd322f3f0bec", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 18}
