ported alongside.\n\nIf you reply with **\"use defaults\"** I will lock items 1–7 as written and produce the full design in the next turn. Otherwise, please indicate which items to override.", "evidence": "Observed \"/workspace\" contains only task.json (no repo, no README, no env_check.sh). `env_check.sh` does not exist on disk. No framework installed in `pip3 list`. `nvidia-smi` present at /usr/bin but fails; no /dev/nvidia* devices. Network disabled (curl DNS fails). task.json `documents.track.md` confirms \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\" — confirms this turn must be paper design only. Hardware: 24 vCPU / 125 GiB / 753 GB free, no GPU — listed in environment block of the task and verified. No HF_TOKEN / proxy / CUDA env vars present.", "assumptions": ["MathInstruct is treated as training data only; GSM8K / MATH / AIME test splits are held out and never touched during training.", "\"Zero-shot\" means no in-context exemplars in the prompt; a fixed optional system prompt is permitted if applied identically to both arms.", "Llama 3-70B is gated on Hugging Face; a valid HF_TOKEN and an accepted license are assumed to be available at run time (not at design time).", "LoRA refers to Hu et al. 2022 LoRA used as a PEFT baseline on attention+MLP linear projections, with adapters in bf16 over an NF4 base (QLoRA-style) so it is comparable in memory to Q-BAdam.", "BAdam refers to Luo et al. 2024 \"BAdam: A Memory-Efficient Full Parameter Optimization of Adam\" (ICLR'24), whose authors also released MathInstruct — treating them as the joint reference recipe.", "Public question framing as written (\"BAdam vs LoRA on Llama 3-70B / MathInstruct / zero-shot math\") means a controlled two-arm comparison rather than a benchmark survey; both arms must be matched on data, template, decoding, and token budget."], "uncertainties": ["Whether `pass@1` only is sufficient as the headline metric or `pass@k` (k>=4) is also needed.", "Whether dataset decontaminat