70B?\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Problem & design rationale\\n\\n### 1.1 Research question\\nWill BAdam achieve higher zero-shot math accuracy than LoRA when fine-tuning Llama-3-70B on MathInstruct?\\n\\n### 1.2 Why the comparison is meaningful\\nBAdam (Luo et al., ICLR 2024, *BAdam: A Memory-Efficient Full Parameter Optimization of Adam*) and LoRA (Hu et al., 2022) attack two different bottlenecks:\\n- **LoRA**: keeps activations of the frozen base and trains a low-rank residual. Trainable params O(d\\u00b7r). Memory is in optimizer state, gradients on the **adapter only**, activations of base.\\n- **BAdam**: trains **all 70B parameters** but updates only one *block* per optimizer step, computing Adam-like stats on the active block and **frozen first-moment / zero second-moment** for inactive blocks. Memory is dominated by one block's optimizer state + activations, not the full parameter footprint.\\n\\nBoth can fit Llama-3-70B SFT inside 8\\u00d780 GB with 4-bit base weights and a careful ZeRO-3 schedule. The question is whether full-parameter SFT (BAdam) recovers enough quality headroom over PEFT (LoRA) in zero-shot math to be preferred, holding everything else constant.\\n\\n### 1.3 Threats to validity and design-level mitigations\\n\\n| Threat | Mitigation in this design |\\n|---|---|\\n| Different prompt templates favor one arm | Same raw-completion BOS-prefixed prompt, identical system prompt (None) and stop strings for both arms |\\n| Different decoding confounds | Greedy decoding for `pass@1`; shared sampler for `pass@k` (`temperature=0.7, top_p=0.95`) |\\n| Decontamination of MathInstruct vs benchmark test items | 8- and 13-gram decontamination filter applied to training set before SFT; offending items dropped and counted |\\n| Different quantization recipes favor one arm | Both arms use **identical NF4 (4-bit) base weights** + bf16 trainable buffers; LoRA stays in QLoRA form, BAdam in Q-bitsandbytes-compatible form |\\n| Compute unfairness | Effective batch size and total tokens matched across arms; also log wall-clock so the reader can see any speedup cost |\\n| Seed-picking by luck | Pre-registered seed sets; 3 seeds for headline cells, **6 seeds only on the single locked-in best config per arm** for the confirmatory CI |\\n| Incoherent reporting (per-task vs averaged) | Report per-benchmark primary and a clearly-labeled arithmetic mean only as a coarse summary |\\n| Pre-registered cherry-picking | Locked decision rule in \\u00a77 before any training |\\n\\n### 1.4 Pre-registered pass criterion (headline)\\n**PASS** iff, on the *confirmatory 6-seed runs* on the locked best config of each arm:\\n- \\u0394 pass@1 (BAdam \\u2212 LoRA) is positive **and** the paired bootstrap 95% CI excludes 0 on **at least two** of {GSM8K, MATH, AIME}, **and**\\n- \\u0394 values are not sign-flipped on a low-variance sanity fallback (GSM8K).\\n\\n### 1.5 Pre-registered fail / equivalence rule\\n- **FAIL**: \\u0394 < 0 with 95% CI excluding 0 on GSM8K and AIME **or** \\u0394 < \\u22121.0 pp on MATH.\\n- **EQUIV** (declare \\\"no robust advantage\\\"): |\\u0394| \\u2264 0.5 pp on GSM8K **and** |\\u0394| \\u2264 1.0 pp on MATH with 95% CIs enclosing 0.\\n\\n### 1.6 Out of scope\\n- Inference throughput at fixed accuracy (we report training throughput only).\\n- RLHF / DPO / RFT second-stage.\\n- Non-math benchmarks (MMLU, BBH, etc.).\\n- Multi-node scaling beyond single node.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Treatments (arms)\\n\\n### 2.1 Arm A \\u2014 LoRA (PEFT, baseline)\\n- Adapter injection on **all linear projections in attention and MLP**: `q_proj, k_proj, v_proj, o_proj, gate_proj, up_proj, down_proj`.\\n- Adapter dtype: bf16.\\n- Base weight dtype: **NF4 (4-bit), double-quant off**, computed via `bitsandbytes`.\\n- Sweep cells: `r \\u2208 {16, 64}`, `\\u03b1 = 2\\u00b7r`, dropout `0.05`. So two cells per arm.\\n- Optimizer: AdamW on adapter parameters only; betas `(0.9, 0.999)`, weight decay `0.0`, eps `1e-8`.\\n\\n### 2.2 Arm B \\u2014 BAdam (memory-efficient full-FT)\\n- All 70B parameters trainable, base weight NF4 (matched to Arm A).\\n- Optimizer: BAdam; block size = **layer-wise fine-grained** (each Transformer block's Q/K/V/O/MLP linear forms one block \\u2014 paper's main recipe).\\n- Sweep cell: stages-per-step `s \\u2208 {1, 2, 4}`. Three cells.\\n- BAdam LR sweep `{5e-6, 1e-5, 2e-5}` chosen by first-pass validation on GSM8K-train-100-sample held-out (also applied to LoRA at LR `{1e-4, 2e-4}` to keep sweeps symmetric in cardinality).\\n\\n### 2.3 Matched invariants across arms (single source of truth)\\n\\n| Invariant | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Base model | `meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-70B` (base, **not** Instruct \\u2014 SFT is what we are measuring) |\\n| Tokenizer | Meta-Llama-3 tokenizer, BOS-prefixed raw completion format |\\n| Quantization | NF4 base, bf16 trainable buffers |\\n| Training data | `TsinghuaC3I/MathInstruct` post-decontamination |\\n| Optimizer family | Adam-flavored (LoRA: AdamW; BAdam: BAdam) |\\n| LR schedule | cosine, 3% warmup, 1 epoch |\\n| Sequence length | 2048 packed |\\n| Effective batch size | 64 sequences \\u00d7 2048 tokens = **131,072 tokens / micro-batch**; **gradient accumulation 4 \\u21d2 524,288 tokens / optimizer step** |\\n| Total tokens seen | identical across arms \\u2248 MathInstruct ~262k \\u00d7 ~1k tokens \\u2248 **260M tokens** \\u2248 **~500 optimizer steps** (1 epoch) |\\n| Seeds per cell | 3 (`{1, 2, 3}`) for sweep |\\n| Confirmatory seeds | 6 (`{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}`) on best cell of each arm |\\n| Hardware | 1 node \\u00d7 8\\u00d780 GB A100/H100 |\\n| Parallelism | FSDP / DeepSpeed **ZeRO-3**; for BAdam, offload inactive blocks to CPU pinned memory with prefetch (CPU offload is a **logged flag**, not default) |\\n| Precision math | bf16 forward/backward; FP32 master for trainable buffers |\\n| Random | torch `seed_everything`, deterministic algorithms on where supported; CUDA backend deterministic |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Data\\n\\n### 3.1 Training data\\n- Source: `TsinghuaC3I/MathInstruct`. Treat **262k mixed-sample partition** as canonical; subset packaged as `MathInstruct.json` and `MathInstruct.parquet`. Use the *training split* only.\\n- Tokenize with the Llama-3 tokenizer; pack to `seq_len=2048` with `DataCollatorForLanguageModeling(mlm=False)` and `group_by_length=True`.\\n- Format: `{\\\"instruction\\\": ..., \\\"input\\\": ..., \\\"output\\\": ...}` \\u2192 concatenated as `BOS + instruction + input + output + EOS`; loss is computed **only on the `output` tokens** to match standard SFT practice. Same masking for both arms.\\n\\n### 3.2 Decontamination\\n- Build n-gram sets of test items from **GSM8K test (1319)**, **MATH test (5000)**, **AIME 2020\\u20132025 (180 problems)**.\\n- Token 8-grams and 13-grams (whitespace-tokenized).\\n- For every MathInstruct training item, drop it iff any 13-gram from test items appears; record drops; require post-filter training set to lose **no more than 5%** of items; if > 5%, raise and refine to a 20-gram filter as a fallback.\\n- Report `n_train_before`, `n_train_after`, drop rate per source benchmark.\\n\\n### 3.3 Held-out evaluation\\n- **GSM8K** test split, 1319 items. Answer is a single integer; primary metric is strict exact-match after extraction.\\n- **MATH** test split, 5000 items; primary metric exact-match with `\\\\boxed{...}` extractor (sympy equivalence on rendered expressions as secondary).\\n- **AIME** (2020\\u20132025) \\u2248 180 items; primary metric exact-match on integer answer; reported but **not** used as a pass-criterion benchmark because of high variance at small N (we do require AIME to be reported; threshold rule is GSM/MATH only).\\n- **No few-shot exemplars** in any prompt. The single system-level instruction (identical across arms) is left as `None` per the locked prompt choice \\u2014 pure zero-shot, BOS-prefixed completion.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Training recipe\\n\\n### 4.1 Tokenization & packing\\n- Llama-3 BPE; sequence length 2048; packing `Seq2SeqTrainer`'s `group_by_length=True`. Mask the `instruction+input` part of the loss.\\n\\n### 4.2 Per-arm hyperparameters\\n\\n**Arm A \\u2014 LoRA**\\n| Hyperparam | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| `r` | 16, 64 |\\n| `lora_alpha` | 2r |\\n| `lora_dropout` | 0.05 |\\n| target_modules | q,k,v,o,gate,up,down |\\n| learning_rate | {1e-4, 2e-4} (3-seed sweep) \\u2014 best cell locked, then 6-seed confirmatory |\\n| batch micro | 64 seq \\u00d7 2048 tok |\\n| grad accum | 4 |\\n| warmup | 3% of steps |\\n| cosine to 0 | yes |\\n| weight decay | 0.0 on adapters |\\n| beta1, beta2 | 0.9, 0.999 |\\n| eps | 1e-8 |\\n| gradient checkpointing | on |\\n\\n**Arm B \\u2014 BAdam**\\n| Hyperparam | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| block scheme | per-transformer-layer fine-grained |\\n| stages s | 1, 2, 4 (3-seed sweep) \\u2014 best s locked, then 6-seed confirmatory |\\n| learning_rate | {5e-6, 1e-5, 2e-5} (3-seed sweep) |\\n| batch micro | 64 seq \\u00d7 2048 tok |\\n| grad accum | 4 |\\n| warmup | 3% of steps |\\n| cosine to 0 | yes |\\n| beta1, beta2 | 0.9, 0.999 |\\n| eps | 1e-8 |\\n| gradient checkpointing | on |\\n| ZeRO-3 offload of inactive blocks | off (default); **flag** for 1\\u00d780 GB fallback |\\n\\n### 4.3 Parallelism and precision\\n- DeepSpeed ZeRO-3, `bf16_enabled`, `fp32_master_weights_and_grads`.\\n- For BAdam: ZeRO-3 partitions parameters; `param_offload=False` by default (all 70B in HBM as fp32 master \\u2248 280 GB is too large; therefore BAdam only updates the master for the **active block**, and uses bf16 for the trainable active block only \\u2014 this is the published BAdam memory model).\\n\\n### 4.4 Hardware target\\n8\\u00d780 GB A100 or H100, NVLink, single node. **CPU offload is treated as a logged contingency**, not the default.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Decoding & evaluation\\n\\n### 5.1 Greedy `pass@1`\\n- Decoding: `do_sample=False`, `temperature=1.0` ignored, `max_new_tokens=2048`, `min_new_tokens=1`, stop on EOS or `\\\\boxed{...}` close + newline.\\n- Apply **identical post-processing** for both arms: extract the last `\\\\boxed{...}` content; fallback to last integer for GSM8K/AIME; sympy equivalence fallback for MATH.\\n- Run on every benchmark's full test set.\\n\\n### 5.2 `pass@k` with sampling\\n- `temperature=0.7, top_p=0.95, n=8, max_new_tokens=2048`. Estimate `pass@8` unbiased per Chen et al. 2021.\\n- Also `pass@4` for cost discipline.\\n\\n### 5.3 Evaluator\\n- All evaluations go through a single harness (we'll use HuggingFace `lm-evaluation-harness` with `math` task template, or `math_eval` from MathInstruct repo, **whichever is used must be identical for both arms** \\u2014 choose once, freeze, do not swap mid-experiment).\\n- Evaluator software version pinned (see \\u00a78).\\n\\n### 5.4 Reporting metrics\\n- Per benchmark, per arm, per cell:\\n  - `pass@1` (mean \\u00b1 std over seeds)\\n  - `pass@4`, `pass@8`\\n- \\u0394 pass@1 (BAdam \\u2212 LoRA), 95% paired bootstrap CI over seeds, 10 000 resamples.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Efficiency / cost reporting\\n\\nBAdam's claim is *quality at LoRA-like cost*, so this comparison is meaningless without efficiency columns. **Required** for both arms:\\n\\n| Quantity | How measured |\\n|---|---|\\n| Peak GPU memory per GPU (MiB) | `torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated(device)` after warmup and again at step 100, 500, end of step |\\n| Tokens / optimizer step | identical by design (invariant table) |\\n| Tokens / sec / GPU | measured over 100 steady steps excluding first 20 warmup |\\n| Wall-clock to 260M training tokens | from first forward to last evaluation; reported per arm |\\n| Total CPU offload traffic | bytes transferred CPU\\u2194GPU per step (only BAdam if offload flag is on) |\\n| EMA snapshot cost | keep last-3 checkpoints, suffix-average pass@1 (reported as `EMA-3` ablation only, **not** as headline) |\\n| Effective parameter count | LoRA: \\u03a3(r \\u00b7 d_in + r \\u00b7 d_out); BAdam: 70B |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Statistical analysis\\n\\n- **Confirmatory** statistics use only the 6-seed runs on the **locked best cell** of each arm.\\n- Per benchmark: `\\u0394\\u0302 = mean(BAdam_pass@1) \\u2212 mean(LoRA_pass@1)`, paired by seed.\\n- 95% CI from 10,000 paired bootstrap resamples.\\n- Holm\\u2013Bonferroni correction across the three benchmarks for the **pass criterion** (GSM8K, MATH, AIME) \\u2014 applies only to the confirmatory test, not the headline arithmetic mean.\\n- **Decision rule**:\\n  - **PASS**: \\u0394\\u0302 > 0 and CI excludes 0 on at least 2 of {GSM8K, MATH} *after* Holm correction.\\n  - **FAIL**: \\u0394\\u0302 < 0 and CI excludes 0 on GSM8K *or* \\u0394\\u0302 < \\u22121.0 pp on MATH.\\n  - **EQUIV**: |\\u0394\\u0302| \\u2264 0.5 pp on GSM8K *and* |\\u0394\\u0302| \\u2264 1.0 pp on MATH *and* both CIs include 0.\\n  - Otherwise, \\\"inconclusive; report all numbers\\\" \\u2014 no claim either way.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Reproducibility\\n\\n- Lock `transformers==4.43.x`, `peft==0.11.x`, `trl==0.10.x`, `bitsandbytes==0.43.x`, `accelerate==0.33.x`, `datasets==2.20.x`, `torch==2.4.x`, `deepspeed==0.15.x`, `vllm==0.5.x` (for eval only).\\n- Random seeds: `{1,2,3,4,5,6}`. Seeds are set in `torch`, `numpy`, `random`, `transformers.set_seed`. `CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG=:4096:8` and `torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True, warn_only=True)` where supported.\\n- Base checkpoint SHA pinned: `meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-70B` revision id recorded.\\n- MathInstruct data SHA pinned via `datasets` `download_checksums` or parquet hash recorded.\\n- Three checkpoints per arm retained (last + 2 best by validation `pass@1` on a 256-item held-out slice of MathInstruct). No test-set hyperparameter selection.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Final result tables (templates to be filled in by the runner)\\n\\n**Table 9.A \\u2014 Confirmatory (6-seed, best cell, \\u00b1 std)**\\n| | GSM8K | MATH | AIME |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| LoRA (best cell) | `m\\u00b1s` | `m\\u00b1s` | `m\\u00b1s` |\\n| BAdam (best cell) | `m\\u00b1s` | `m\\u00b1s` | `m\\u00b1s` |\\n| \\u0394\\u0302 (BAdam \\u2212 LoRA) | `\\u0394\\u0302 [CI_lo, CI_hi]` | `\\u0394\\u0302 [CI_lo, CI_hi]` | `\\u0394\\u0302 [CI_lo, CI_hi]` |\\n\\n**Table 9.B \\u2014 Efficiency**\\n| | Peak GPU mem (GiB) | Tok/s/GPU | Wall-clock to 260M tokens | Offload flag |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| LoRA (best r) | | | | n/a |\\n| BAdam (best s) | | | | on/off |\\n\\n**Table 9.C \\u2014 Sweep ablation (3 seeds; informational, not confirmatory)**\\n- LoRA: `r \\u2208 {16, 64}`, GSM8K pass@1 each.\\n- BAdam: `s \\u2208 {1, 2, 4}`, GSM8K pass@1 each.\\n- Used only to identify the cell that goes into 9.A.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Risks and contingencies\\n\\n| Risk | Contingency |\\n|---|---|\\n| MathInstruct requires HF auth or is rate-limited | Fall back to mirror; in the worst case, use the decontaminated subset from the original WizardMath paper repo (same authors) |\\n| `deepspeed` + BAdam integration friction | Implement BAdam as a thin \\\"block-frozen Adam\\\" wrapper around `bitsandbytes` 4-bit params + ZeRO-3, replicating the reference paper's release behavior |\\n| 70B + ZeRO-3 still OOM on a node | Activate CPU offload flag for BAdam only; LoRA unaffected. Log the OOM as a measured finding |\\n| Evaluation harness gives different answers than expected on small samples | Use sympy equivalence as a secondary metric on MATH and report it as a robustness column, not as a decision column |\\n| Holm correction kills a marginal PASS | Switch to the un-corrected 95% CI **only** if the researcher pre-approves that relaxation in writing (defer to researcher) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Decision rule (final, single sentence)\\n\\n> Report PASS / FAIL / EQUIV / Inconclusive based on the locked pass criterion (\\u00a71.4), fail rule (\\u00a71.5), and statistical protocol (\\u00a77), using only the confirmatory 6-seed runs on each arm's locked best cell \\u2014 no other statistic, no other cell, and no other seed count is permitted to drive the claim.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Appendix A \\u2014 Software stack pinned\\n\\n```\\ntransformers==4.43.x, peft==0.11.x, trl==0.10.x,\\nbitsandbytes==0.43.x, accelerate==0.33.x, datasets==2.20.x,\\ntorch==2.4.x + CUDA 12.1, deepspeed==0.15.x, vllm==0.5.x (eval only),\\nnumpy==1.26.x, sympy==1.12.x, scipy==1.13.x, scikit-learn==1.5.x\\n```\\n\\nThe runtime bubblewrap in this design-only phase has **none of these installed and no GPU**; the design above assumes they are installed on the dedicated SFT/eval cluster.\\n\\n## Appendix B \\u2014 Items deferred to the researcher\\n\\nNone for the design itself. The next concrete act (execution) requires an HF_TOKEN, a feasible GPU reservation, and pre-approved decontamination thresholds locked.\", \"evidence\": \"Same environment inspection used in the plan: /workspace has only task.json; no env_check.sh exists anywhere; no DL packages installed (PyTorch / Transformers / PEFT / trl / bitsandbytes / vLLM / accelerate / datasets / DeepSpeed / NumPy / SymPy / tiktoken / tokenizers / safetensors / huggingface_hub / wandb absent); no /dev/nvidia* and nvidia-smi binary fails; DNS for huggingface.co does not resolve, no HF_TOKEN / proxy / CUDA env vars set; 24 vCPU, 125 GiB RAM, 753 GB free on /workspace. task.json `documents.track.md` confirms \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\" \\u2014 this handoff is therefore a paper design, not an executed experiment. The seven items in \\\"Items deferred\\\" from the plan were explicitly approved by the researcher with the defaults I proposed (base Llama-3-70B, MathInstruct, BOS raw-completion zero-shot, 3-seed sweep with 6-seed frozen best-config confirmatory CI, 8x80 GB + ZeRO-3 with CPU-offload flag, 8- and 13-gram decontamination, tokens-matched primary with wall-clock alongside).\", \"assumptions\": [\"Researcher-approved defaults used throughout: llama-3-70B base, MathInstruct as training set, BOS-prefixed raw-completion zero-shot prompt, 3-seed sweep + 6-seed confirmatory on locked best cell, 8x80 GB + DeepSpeed ZeRO-3, 8/13-gram decontamination, tokens-matched primary baseline with wall-clock reported.\", \"MathInstruct is treated as training data only; GSM8K / MATH / AIME test splits are held out and never touched during training.\", \"\\\"Zero-shot\\\" means no in-context exemplars in the prompt; the system prompt is fixed to None across both arms.\", \"Llama-3-70B is gated on Hugging Face; a valid HF_TOKEN and license acceptance are assumed at run time but not required at design time.\", \"LoRA is implemented in the QLoRA style (4-bit NF4 base + bf16 adapters) so it is memory-comparable to BAdam.\", \"BAdam refers to Luo et al. 2024, block-wise Adam with parameter blocks progressively activated per step; stages s is the per-step activation count.\", \"CPU offload of inactive BAdam blocks is logged as a contingency flag, not the default, on 8x80 GB.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether sympy-equivalence fallback on MATH should be a co-primary metric or only a robustness column \\u2014 currently treated as the latter.\", \"Whether evaluator should be lm-eval-harness or math_eval; design freezes one choice pre-experiment and is indifferent afterwards.\", \"Whether Holm correction relaxes to none if the PASS criterion is marginal \\u2014 design requires explicit researcher pre-approval.\", \"If AIME proves too small/variable, whether to drop AIME from the PASS criterion entirely \\u2014 currently AIME is reported but not part of the PASS trigger.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-cad5c813-d31a-4ae1-bae0-e895bc6ae43f", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 23}
